From 43a1c1f3fd5f9defb30dab44c82824b94bb5bbf5 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Egbert de Pauw <egbert@despaankamer.nl>
Date: Sun, 15 Nov 2026 16:33:06 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] Fix missing Shearwater dives after a deleted dive

When a dive is deleted on a Shearwater dive computer, its manifest
record stays in place with the header 0x5A23. The manifest loop skips
those records and counts them, but appends only the first count *
RECORD_SIZE bytes of the page to the manifest buffer. With deleted
records in the page, the last records before the stop point are cut
off, and every valid dive among them is never downloaded. That is up
to one dive for every deleted record in the same manifest page: the
oldest new dives on an incremental download, or the last dives of a
full page on a full download.

Append all records up to the current offset instead, including the
deleted ones. The download loop already skips the deleted records.
---
 src/shearwater_petrel.c | 7 +++++--
 1 file changed, 5 insertions(+), 2 deletions(-)

diff --git a/src/shearwater_petrel.c b/src/shearwater_petrel.c
index c1cc880..734e43c 100644
--- a/src/shearwater_petrel.c
+++ b/src/shearwater_petrel.c
@@ -292,8 +292,11 @@ shearwater_petrel_device_foreach (dc_device_t *abstract, dc_dive_callback_t call
 		current += 1;
 		maximum -= RECORD_COUNT - count - deleted;
 
-		// Append the manifest records to the main buffer.
-		if (!dc_buffer_append (manifests, data, count * RECORD_SIZE)) {
+		// Append the manifest records to the main buffer. The deleted
+		// records are included, because they can be interleaved with
+		// the valid ones. They are skipped again when the dives are
+		// downloaded.
+		if (!dc_buffer_append (manifests, data, offset)) {
 			ERROR (abstract->context, "Insufficient buffer space available.");
 			dc_buffer_free (buffer);
 			dc_buffer_free (manifests);
